<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chevalier de Chaumont</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1640">1640</a>–<a href="/years/1710">1710</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Alexandre de Chaumont</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alexandre, Chevalier de Chaumont, was a French naval officer and diplomat who led <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xiv">Louis XIV</a>'s first embassy to King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/narai">Narai</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ayutthaya-kingdom">Ayutthaya</a> in 1685. He was instructed to seek the king's conversion to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a>, which Narai politely declined, but the embassy won privileges for French missionaries and was followed by a Siamese embassy to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/versailles">Versailles</a> in 1686.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chevalier-de-chaumont.jpg" alt="Chevalier de Chaumont" width="320" height="426" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jean-Baptiste Nolin · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Audience_with_Narai,_1685-10-18_(b).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
